T17:06:14Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":"resolved","sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"- **OS version and name**:  Windows 10 Pro, version 1803, build 17134.112<!-- Replace with version + name -->\r\n- **Poetry version**: 0.11.2\r\n- **Link of a [Gist](https://gist.github.com/) with the contents of your pyproject.toml file**: [pyproject.toml](https://gist.github.com/RaptDept/55ce98fe2bc1b1a58053fed26f59e4f4) <!-- Gist Link Here -->\r\n\r\n## Issue\r\n<!-- Now feel free to write your issue, but please be descriptive! Thanks again 🙌 ❤️ -->\r\nIf you look at my gist above, my project's pyproject.toml specifies a local path dependency that also contains its own (poetry) pyproject.toml. Non-optional dependencies and dev-dependencies in this secondary pyproject.toml get installed just fine, but dependencies specified in its extras (which *have* to be optional or else poetry complains about it) that are explicitly requested by the first project don't get installed at all.\r\n\r\nI did some debugging and digging into poetry's source and found that DirectoryDependency._package.extras is always an empty dict. Inserting `self._package.extras = package.extras` in the block below gets rid of this issue, but I'm not sure if this is the correct approach. \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/sdispater/poetry/blob/1b7492e5659a43c0a05f10c6d60e90603c6c3406/poetry/packages/directory_dependency.py#L66-L81","closed_by":{"login":"sdispater","id":555648,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NTY0OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/555648?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdispater","html_url":"https://github.com/sdispater","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdispater/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdispater/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api